---
version: 2.0.2
title: testing: a typed rule silent over a definition girard couldn't type
file: ./test/grice/testing_test.gleam
test_name: render_shows_the_coverage_of_a_typed_run_test
---
-- src/app.gleam
pub fn main() {
  let _ = 1 + "one"
}
-- output
note[grice/untyped-definition]: Can't infer the types of this definition
  ┌─ src/app.gleam:1:1
  │
1 │ pub fn main() {
  │ ^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^ girard couldn't type this definition

girard couldn't type `main`: type mismatch: Int vs String. Typed rules get
no answers about the code inside it, so they may miss problems there.

Hint: If `gleam build` accepts this code, it's a gap in girard, the type
inference grice uses, so please report it at
https://github.com/alvivi/girard/issues.

1 note in 1 module.
Coverage is incomplete: 1 definition in 1 module couldn't be typed, so
typed rules didn't see all of the code.

